    urgentTag: { en: 'URGENT' },
    urgentHead: { en: 'Act this week' },
    urgentBody: { en: "You are on a deadline. A letter asking you to respond to concerns is the last chance to change an officer's mind before a decision. The window is short and it does not extend. If the letter uses the word misrepresentation, treat it as the most serious immigration document you will ever receive." },
    urgentBring: { en: 'the letter, every page · a copy of what you originally submitted · any correspondence since' },
    refusalTag: { en: 'REFUSAL' },
    refusalHead: { en: 'Time sensitive' },
    refusalBody: { en: 'Find out why before you do anything else. Refusal letters cite a provision and tick a box. They do not tell you what the officer actually concluded. Reapplying without knowing is the most expensive mistake in immigration — and appeal deadlines run whether or not you have decided.' },
    refusalBring: { en: 'your refusal letter · a copy of your application · your passport and status documents' },
    hcTag: { en: 'H&C' },
    hcHead: { en: 'Worth a conversation' },
    hcBody: { en: 'Your years here may count for more than you think. Work, rent, taxes, school, community — none of it counts under the ordinary programmes. Under a humanitarian and compassionate application it is the whole case. What goes into that file, and how it is argued, decides the outcome.' },
    hcBring: { en: 'anything showing time in Canada — pay stubs, leases, tax slips · documents for any children here · any past immigration paperwork' },
    sponsorTag: { en: 'SPONSORSHIP' },
    sponsorHead: { en: 'Plan it properly' },
    sponsorBody: { en: 'Sponsorship turns on evidence, not paperwork. The scrutiny is not personal — it is how these files are screened. Relationships that do not fit a standard template draw more of it. The evidence can be built deliberately instead of scrambled together after a request arrives.' },
    sponsorBring: { en: 'marriage or relationship documents · proof of your status in Canada · anything showing the history of your relationship' },
    healthTag: { en: 'HEALTHCARE' },
    healthHead: { en: 'Two clocks to manage' },
    healthBody: { en: 'Immigration and licensing are separate systems. Your right to enter is decided by immigration authorities. Your right to practise is decided by a provincial regulator. Different requirements, different timelines, no obligation to coordinate. Almost every disappointment comes from planning one and assuming the other follows.' },
    healthBring: { en: 'your credentials and any assessment you have started · language test results, if taken · any job offer or recruiter correspondence' },
    bizTag: { en: 'ENTREPRENEUR' },
    bizHead: { en: 'Check before you commit' },
    bizBody: { en: 'Choose the route before you spend the capital. Nobody can guarantee permanent residence — not a lawyer, not a consultancy with offices in three cities. If you have been given that guarantee in writing, bring it. It tells us a great deal about the rest of the offer.' },
    bizBring: { en: 'business registration and financials · any proposal or quote you have received · your passport and travel history' },
    generalTag: { en: 'GENERAL' },
