      openquote: { en: "Difficult and hopeless are not the same thing. Usually it means nobody has looked at the file properly yet." },
      heading1: { en: "The forms are free." },
      heading2: { en: "The mistakes cost years." },
      intro: { en: "Anyone can download an application. That's not the hard part, and it's not where files fail. They fail in the same handful of ways, over and over, and almost all of them are invisible until it's far too late to fix." },
      r1l: { en: "The family member you didn't declare." },
      r1b: { en: "A child from an earlier relationship. A spouse you're separated from but never divorced. Leave them off, and you may be barred from ever sponsoring them. People find out a decade later." },
      r2l: { en: "One wrong answer becomes misrepresentation." },
      r2b: { en: "A date, a job title, a refusal from another country you forgot to mention. A finding can carry a multi-year bar — and it attaches to you, not to that application. Often it's an agent who wrote it on a form you signed without reading." },
      r3l: { en: "Reapplying without knowing why you were refused." },
      r3b: { en: "The letter cites a provision and ticks a box. It never says what the officer actually thought. So people fix the wrong thing, pay twice, wait twice, and build a refusal history." },
      r4l: { en: "The deadline nobody told you was running." },
      r4b: { en: "Appeal periods are short and fixed. They run from the decision, not from the day you felt ready to deal with it. Once gone, gone." },
      r5l: { en: "A birthday." },
      r5b: { en: "Dependency locks at the date the application is received. Six months spent gathering documents can age a child out of your family's application permanently." },
      r6l: { en: "The person who wasn't licensed." },
      r6b: { en: "They file things in your name you never see. When it collapses they're unreachable, the misrepresentation is yours, and there's no regulator to complain to — because they weren't regulated." },
      close1: { en: "None of that is bad luck. Every one is preventable, and most are preventable in the first hour of someone looking at the file properly." },
